  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🗿 World of Warcraft Troll Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Troll names with the snap of Vol'jin and Zul'jin, and a tribe to call home."
    },
    "intro": "Warcraft's trolls have names you can hear in your head: Vol'jin, Sen'jin, Zul'jin, Rastakhan, Talanji. Many are two short parts joined by an apostrophe, and \"jin\" turns up again and again. This **World of Warcraft troll name generator** builds names in that style, and can add one of Azeroth's troll tribes.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How troll names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Two parts and an apostrophe:</strong> Vol'jin, Sen'jin, Zul'jin. The second part is often short and repeated across names, especially <em>-jin</em>.</li><li><strong>Or one strong word:</strong> Rastakhan, Talanji, Zalazane, Rokhan.</li><li><strong>Hard, clipped sounds:</strong> z, j, k and r, with open vowels.</li></ul><p>The generator mixes both kinds, so you get names like Zal'tik and Kozzul. All are new names, not ones from the game.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "The troll tribes",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Darkspear:</strong> the tribe of Sen'jin and Vol'jin, who joined the Horde.</li><li><strong>Zandalari:</strong> the ancient troll empire, ruled by King Rastakhan and later Queen Talanji; playable since Battle for Azeroth.</li><li><strong>Amani:</strong> the forest trolls of Zul'Aman, Zul'jin's people, long-time enemies of the <a href=\"elf-name-generator.html\">elves</a>.</li><li><strong>Gurubashi:</strong> the jungle trolls of Stranglethorn and Zul'Gurub.</li><li><strong>Drakkari:</strong> the ice trolls of Northrend.</li></ul><p>The <em>With a tribe</em> format adds one of these or other troll tribes from the games, like the Sandfury, Bloodscalp, Witherbark and Smolderthorn.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Getting a free name in WoW",
        "content": "<p>WoW names are one word with no apostrophes, so Zal'tik becomes Zaltik in game. Most trolls worship the loa, the spirit-gods of the troll empires, and a troll character's chosen loa makes a good starting point for their story.</p><p>For other Warcraft races, see the <a href=\"night-elf-name-generator.html\">Night Elf</a>, <a href=\"blood-elf-name-generator.html\">Blood Elf</a> and <a href=\"wow-orc-name-generator.html\">Orc</a> name generators.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are some good WoW troll names?",
        "answer": "Two short parts with an apostrophe, like Vol'jin or Zul'jin, or a single strong word like Rastakhan. In game you'll need to drop the apostrophe."
      },
      {
        "question": "What troll tribes are there in Warcraft?",
        "answer": "The best known are the Darkspear, Zandalari, Amani, Gurubashi and Drakkari, plus smaller tribes like the Sandfury and Bloodscalp."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are these names from the game?",
        "answer": "No. They're new names in the same style."
      }
    ]
